1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7. Be2 Nc6 8. O-O O-O 9. Nb3 Be6 10. f4 Qc8 11. h3 Rd8 12. Bf3 b5 $2 {Aitken} 13. Nd5 (13. Nxb5 Bc4) 13... Nd7 14. c3 f5 15. exf5 gxf5 16. Na5 $1 {Aitken} Ndb8 17. Qe2 (17. Nxe7+ Nxe7 18. Bxa8 {looks OK. It appears Aitken preferred activity to the exchange and a pawn. He does not mention it or tag it with a ?}) 17... Qd7 18. Nxc6 Nxc6 19. Qxb5 Rac8 20. Qe2 Bf7 21. Bf2 e5 22. fxe5 dxe5 23. Ne3 e4 24. Bh5 f4 25. Bxf7+ Qxf7 26. Bg3 f3 27. gxf3 Rd3 28. Rad1 Qg6 29. Kh2 Rcd8 30. Rxd3 exd3 31. Qd2 Kh8 32. f4 Rg8 33. Rg1 h5 34. Rg2 Qe4 35. Qd1 Qh7 36. Bh4 Re8 37. Qf3 Ne7 38. Rg5 Bh6 39. Re5 Qg6 40. Bxe7 Rg8 41. Bg5 d2 42. Rd5 h4 43. Rxd2 Bxg5 {Aitken has this marked as the first time control} 44. fxg5 Qxg5 45. Rg2 Qe5+ 46. Kh1 Re8 47. Qg4 {Good fun game to skip through. Black kept setting one and two move traps, Aitken dodged them matching trick for trick. GC. Source: Aitken Book 37} 1-0

